{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765613,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Pravaran - HR Event ","festival_id":521442,"organization_id":1076204,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-19T16:03:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/pravaran-hr-event-nisadya-national-institute-of-technology-nit-tiruchirappalli-1765613","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Round 1 (Unstop): HR MindSpark (Online Quiz):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Participants will attempt a time-bound quiz covering:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Basic HR concepts and terminology<\/li>\n<li>Workplace and organizational scenarios<\/li>\n<li>Logical thinking and aptitude<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>This round tests how well participants understand the foundation of Human Resource Management. Shortlisted teams will move on to the next round.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Duration: 35 Minutes:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: People Puzzle (HR Case Study):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will be given a realistic HR case involving challenges such as hiring, employee retention, performance management, or workplace conflict. Teams must analyze the situation, identify the key issues, and develop practical and strategic HR solutions.<\/p>\n<p>Teams need to submit their documents within deadline and the teams shortlisted for the 3rd round will have their presentations held offline. The round will assess analytical ability, HR knowledge, strategic thinking, teamwork, and clarity of thought.<\/p>\n<p>Detailed case instructions, submission guidelines, and evaluation criteria will be shared along with the case study.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Structures:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will be given a realistic HR case study.<\/li>\n<li>The case may involve issues like hiring challenges, employee retention, performance management, or workplace conflict.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must analyze the situation and propose clear, practical HR solutions within a limited time.<\/li>\n<li>This round evaluates analytical ability, teamwork, and clarity of thought.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3: HR Negotiation Arena (offline):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams of Round 2 will have their presentations offline.<\/p>\n<p>Teams shortlisted from Round 2 will present their case solutions offline before moving into an engaging HR negotiation challenge. Participants will navigate workplace scenarios, negotiate strategically, and make critical HR decisions under pressure.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must consist of 2-4 members.<\/li>\n<li>All team members must be from the same college.<\/li>\n<li>No limit on the number of teams from each college.<\/li>\n<li>All undergraduate and post-graduate students are eligible to participate.<\/li>\n<li>A person can register as part of only one team for one event. Violation of this rule will lead to disqualification of the entire team.Submission of videos\/ presentations will not be accepted post the deadline.<\/li>\n<li>Certificates to all participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to Engineering Students, MBA Students, UG, PG<\/li>\n<li>Team Participation, Team Size: 2-4 Members<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are not allowed<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Disclaimer:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Third Place for an event will be awarded only if the number of participating teams is six or more for that event.<\/li>\n<li>All decisions, modifications, and changes related to the event rest solely with the Organizing Committee, and their decision shall be final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":29663114,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-04T14:13:04+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-05T18:42:48+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":nu